hey guys it's Jan here I've been to see  Star Wars The Force awakens and I can  tell you right now that it kicks off the  new sequel trilogy in super fine form  it's a really emotional movie in all  sorts of ways in fact there were several  very different occasions when I felt  myself welling up even a new hope gave  us three young stars who worked so  beautifully together and the force  awakens repeats the magic with the  brilliant casting of Daisy Ridley John  boyega and Oscar Isaac after the  disappointment of Natalie Portman's  character Padme in the prequels it's  great to see a fantastic and interesting  female character who actually gets to do  stuff rather than sit around and were  5,000 different hairstyles Ridley's come  from being on almost no one's radar  having appeared in a few British TV  shows to being the center of a whole  galaxy and let me tell you she is on  foreign formers ray managing to play  each scene to its full potential whether  that's big action set-pieces heroes  exchanges or more subdued or tender  moments and the on-screen chemistry is  superb between her and John boyega who  plays stormtrooper Finn boyega burst  onto the big screen in the alien  invasion action comedy attack the block  and followed that up with performances  in a number of indie films including a  terrific turn in the Sundance Award  winner Imperial dreams and he really  looks like he's having an absolute blast  on the force awakens he's got a real  gift for comedy and he has some fabulous  scenes with Harrison Ford but he's also  just as good when it's drama action or a  touch of vulnerability that's called for  Oscar Isaacs been turning in some  absolutely stonking performances over  the past few years from the coen  brothers movie inside Llewyn Davis to  the superlatives IFI flick ex machina  and he's definitely on point as x-wing  Squadron Leader Poe Dameron who gets a  nice mix of action and humorous dialogue  Adam driver who's best known for the HBO  show girls is brilliant as kylo Ren and  get some suitably dramatic moments and  it was pretty cool seeing him wield his  spiti crossguard lightsaber I really  felt spoiled for amazing actors in  episode 7 another of them being Donal  Gleeson who you may have seen over the  past 12  months in movies like ex machina  Brooklyn and unbroken as general Hux  Gleason puts in a fantastically  fanatical performance Gwendoline  Christie so incredible as the badass  Brienne in Game of Thrones there was a  little disappointed that she didn't  feature a bit more as Captain phasma in  the force awakens though she did a good  job when she is on screen the king of  performance capture Andy Serkis plays  the intriguing and rather mysterious  Supreme Leader Snoke and also appearing  by a performance capture Lupita Nyong'o  puts in a charming turn as the ancient  alien pirate Maz Kanata by the way if  you're a fan of the awesome Indonesia  martial arts movie the raid look out for  its stars and fight choreographer Zico  you a and the iron rien who get a cool  little scene in the movie and of course  it's so good to see Harrison Ford Carrie  Fisher and Mark Hamill backers Han Leia  and Luke there are some really heartfelt  moments between han and Leia and when we  first see Ford and Fisher on screen it  feels like they return to the world of  Star Wars after all these years gives  added meaning and poignancy to the words  that Leia and Han say to each other and  of course Peter Mayhew and cheerio back  to and what's not to love about that  adorable worky there's some lovely  interaction between chewy and Han all of  which is very reminiscent of some of my  favorite moments in the original trilogy  as for the droids I absolutely loved  bb-8 he makes a really wonderful  addition to the franchise and sound  designer a mix of Ben Burtt he's worked  on all the Star Wars movies is on fine  form yet again ensuring that bb-8 is  full of personality and makes a lasting  impression it feels like he's the r2d2  of this new trilogy as for r2d2 himself  there's not as much of him as I'd hoped  but when we do see him it feels like  it's worth waiting for and I can't  forget c-3po who's as funny as ever and  I just love the way he first appears in  the movie classic also returning to the  galaxy far far away is oscar-winning  composer John Williams whose music  really made the original trilogy and  it's a delight to hear him mix and find  new music with his much-loved original  themes and JJ Abrams and composer Lin  Manuel Miranda who created the Broadway  musical Hamilton did really excellent  work with the music on the new Cantina  star seen talking of JJ Abrams here in  lawrence kasdan who wrote The Empire  Strikes Back and Return of the Jedi have  written a script that's a wonderful mix  of action adventure humor heart and  nostalgia there's plenty of Easter eggs  and callbacks to the previous films and  i'll be making a video about that and  I'll add the annotation here when it's  live I felt like the movies 135 minute  run time just flew by props to Abraham's  Kasdan and the film's editors Mary Ann  Brandon and Mary Jo Marquis for keeping  things rattling along the only place i  would have liked it to have taken a  little bit more time was in the cantina  scene as there were so many cool  creatures and some of them just whizzed  by too quickly not giving me enough time  to properly appreciate the incredible  work of Neil Scanlon and his creature  effects team a shout-out also goes to  cinematographer dan Mendell and costume  designer Michael Kaplan who both worked  with Abrams on multiple movies and to  make up department head amanda night and  her team who's no stranger to  blockbusters having worked on all the  Harry Potter movies all of them did  Stella work on the force awakens there's  a ton of thrilling and spectacular  action in the movie thanks to the hard  work of huge teams led by stunt  coordinator Rob inch special effects  supervisor Chris cobalt whose work we  last saw inspector and visual effects  supervisors Michael Mulholland Roger yet  and Nick Shay again the effort that's  gone into all the film's design and sets  is just phenomenal production designers  Rick Carter and Darren guilford and set  decorator loose on Dallas should be  rightfully very happy with the world's  they've created so to sum up the feel  and tone of the force awakens fits  perfectly with episodes 4 to 6 making it  a wonderfully welcome return to the  world of Star Wars it's full of laughter  emotion intrigue action and stunning  visuals basically it's a fantastic  combination of the old and the new with  a superb cast and top-notch work from  the whole crew star wars the force  awakens gets 5 out of 5 flicks now what  are you looking forward to most about  the force awakens or if you've seen it  already what did you think I  nope to know your experiences did you  see it at midnight did you cosplay did  it live up to your expectations and who  are your favorite new characters in the  movie let me know in the comments below  I'm going to be making a video about the  top WTF moments in the movie as well as  an easter egg video and I'll add  annotations for those here as soon as  their live and as always do please like  leave your comments and share this video  and hit that subscribe button for more  videos like this thanks for watching and  see you next time yippee-ki-yay movie  lovers  you
 

